# 3. Screen-by-screen experience

The following is the complete customer-facing architecture, including interaction states, exceptions and recovery behaviour.

## Screen 01 — App launch and session restoration

Purpose: Determine whether the customer can continue immediately.

The app launches into a clean white screen with the Food101 logo centred. No long animation, no compulsory onboarding carousel.

Logic

- Returning user with valid session → Home.
- First-time user → Welcome.
- Expired session → Home as guest where supported; request sign-in when necessary.
- Deep link → Restore session and open the intended dish, restaurant or order.
- Active order → Restore its tracking state in the background.

States: Splash, checking session, first visit, authenticated, guest, offline, session expired, mandatory app update, maintenance.

Edge cases: A user force-closes the app during payment. On relaunch, the system checks payment and order status before showing any option to pay again.

## Screen 02 — Welcome / authentication

# Good food. No waiting around.

Your favourites, delivered.

Continue with phone

Continue as guest

The initial authentication should be phone-number based with an OTP, using the Nigerian `+234` country code as the default when appropriate.

Screens and states: Phone input → OTP entry → verification → success → Home.

Validation: Incorrect number, invalid OTP, expired OTP, resend cooldown, too many attempts, network failure, already-registered account and temporarily blocked verification.

Recovery: Preserve the entered number, allow editing it, display a resend countdown and avoid clearing all OTP digits unnecessarily.

Guest users can browse menus and build baskets. Sign-in can be requested when required for checkout or order communication.

