### Basket rules

The basket should be accessible from the header and a persistent floating basket bar when populated.

The bar should display item count, subtotal and “View basket”. Avoid showing the complete checkout breakdown on every page.

### Basket states

| State               | UX                                                      |
| ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |
| Empty               | Illustration, “Your basket is empty”, Explore food      |
| One item            | Standard basket                                         |
| Multiple items      | Group by dish                                           |
| Item modified       | Recalculate total immediately                           |
| Item removed        | Undo action for a short period                          |
| Minimum order unmet | Explain the amount remaining                            |
| Unavailable item    | Highlight and require removal/replacement               |
| Restaurant closed   | Block immediate checkout; offer scheduling if supported |
| Expired promotion   | Remove discount and show updated total                  |
| Fee recalculation   | Clearly show new totals                                 |
| Basket restore      | Revalidate all items before allowing checkout           |

Do not let a cached basket proceed to payment with stale prices.

